# Project icons are USER data, not repo content: an icon set is named for
# someone's real projects. They live in <userData>/project-icons/ instead
# (~/.config/harbor/project-icons on Linux); see setup/README.md.
#
# This folder stays empty in the repo and is still read at build time, so a fork
# can bundle a generic set on purpose. Ignoring images here keeps a personal set
# from being committed by accident, which is how 53 icons became a privacy
# finding (P-04) and then, when they were removed, took the whole feature with
# them because an icon had nowhere else it could live.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
*.gif
*.svg
